                              ^^^^^^^^
Direct CD is software to write files directly to cd from Explorer etc.

You'll need something like Adaptec EasyCD Creator; this software is
included too (I assume) since you got DirectCD with your cdwriter.
Start it up and use the RH iso image as the Source, use your
cdwriter as the Destination and start burning.. that's all.

> In the archives it mentioned you need 'rockport' extension????

I think you mean Rock Ridge, but this is irrelevant for a ready to roll
ISO image. It's a thing you should do when you make the actual ISO
image,
but since you already have that... :)

Regards,
Antoine


