When Milo is loaded it replaces the firmware image in memory.  When you
shutdown Linux
it falls back to the console IN MEMORY which is Milo.  In order to reload
the alphabios
console into memory (and execute it) press the reset button.  (Power cycling
the system
works, too.)

Eric Ebinger

