> >Oh yeah, except that it doesn't see my PCI cards...  forgot I was testing
> >it via serial console. :-) Specifically the PCI scan works (i.e. /proc/pci
> 
> Hmm are we sure serial console works in first place? Don't mind to try
> again without the serial console?

No, but I'm pretty sure that isn't the problem.  This machine has
no framebuffer.

> >Also, halt() isn't exported to modules even though the call path:
> >  __get_free_pages (include/linux/mm.h:381)  -->
> >  alloc_pages (include/linux/mm.h:365) -->
> >  BUG (include/asm-alpha/page.h:113)
> >now calles halt().  So modules which use get_free_pages and friends
> 
> Strange, it shouldn't call halt, maybe I forgot to change an #if 0 to #if
> 1? I'll check...

It doesn't actually CALL halt(), but the macro does include it.  Since
halt() is a non-exported function this means modules refuse to load
due to unresolved symbol(s).

I personally think there is no real reason to export halt() to
modules - a simpler solution would be to just do something
like "(int *) 0=0;" in page.h:BUG()

-Mitch


